WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.435
-Welcome, welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:04.670
You're here.
You're watching.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.005
Thank you.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.306
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:08.440
Hey, guys. This is fun.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.177
Tomorrow is Earth Day.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.311
Yeah.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.680
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.717
And for everyone who went
a little too hard on 420,

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.118
it's come back to Earth Day.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.520
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.721
That's right,
tomorrow is Earth Day.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.055
Right now, the Earth is like,

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.157
"So I get a day,
but sharks get a week?

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:26.226
I don't understand."

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.861
Well, some news from Washington.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.762
According to a new poll,
Mitch McConnell

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.765
is the least popular senator
in the U.S.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:35.135
with only a 28%
approval rating.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.470
Yeah, well, I think some other
senators feel bad for McConnell.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.873
So they reached out
with words of encouragement.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.908
For example,
Senator James Lankford said...

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.814
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.049
Senator Cory Booker said...

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.821
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.459
And then --

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.894
then Senator
Peter Welch said...

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.533
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:08.835
And Senator Jon Ossoff said...

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.641
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.143
Then Senator
Roger Marshall said...

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.950
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.351
And Senator Bob Menendez said...

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.759
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.093
-People are cruel.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.962
-And finally,
Senator Jon Tester said...

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.070
Wow.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.705
-Wow.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.574
-They're trying to help me.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:49.942
Well, here's some
big political news.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.478 line:0%
I read that President Biden
is planning to announce

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.615 line:0%
his reelection campaign
next week.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.316
Does Biden even need
to campaign?

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.018
I mean, he's run
for president three times.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.321
Who's got to be like, I got to
learn more about this guy.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.124
Yet the announcement
will be early next week,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.825
Biden said before
getting down to business,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.160
"I just want
to enjoy Coachella."

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.362
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.763
Well, speaking of Coachella,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.199 line:0%
today the final weekend
kicked off.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.969 line:0%
Yep, so between Coachella
and the new "Super Mario" movie,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.737
it's been a big month
for mushrooms.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.739
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.076
Yeah, a lot of people
are excited

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.944
for the second weekend
of Coachella.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.178
I actually just saw
an ad for it.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.513
Check this out.

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.949
-This year's Coachella
has the most packed lineup.

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.941
-Wow, that's a lot of letters.
Ba-ba-ba-ba-ba.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.708
[ Humming "Seinfeld" theme ]

00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:58.043
That's the band name?

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.412
[ Laughs ]

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.880
-Hey, guys,
people are talking about this.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.150
I heard that Kylie Jenner and
Timothée Chalamet are dating.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.385
[ Record scratch ]

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:09.188
-Say what?!

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:10.689
-Yes, yes.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.959
Apparently they've been sneaking
around for months,

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.993
with sources saying Kylie
has mostly been

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:17.196
hanging out at his house.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.399
-Say what?!

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.368
-Not only that,
but there are reports

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:26.005
that the two were seen
kissing backstage at Coachella.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.641
-Say what?!

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.775
-And that's not all.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.244
After that, I heard they might
even go on

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.412
a double date with
Kendall Jenner and Bad Bunny.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.515
-Enough, Jimmy.
Enough.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:36.582
I can't take it.

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.384
It's too much gossip.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:47.794 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.163
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:56.268
-Finally I saw that Carnival
band to cruise passengers

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:59.338
because they were caught fishing
from the balcony in their room.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:01.407
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.677
Unfortunately, their room
overlooked the pool,

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:06.679
but they did pretty well.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:07.846
They caught six retirees

00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:09.148
and a crappy magician.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.750
Yeah, we have a great show.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.685
Let's go write some
thank you notes. Come on.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.553
-♪ The man at hand
that rule the school ♪

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.989
♪ And reach and teach the blind
and find a way from A to Z ♪

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.691
♪ And be the most to boast
I'm loud and proud ♪

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.127
♪ The game and reign
that remain ♪

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:24.330
